        "start_xml_ordinal": 18794,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 699,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 357,
        "paragraph_id": null,
        "text": "Furthermore the group velocity and wave celerity for the semi-discrete system become:"
      },
      {
        "container_path": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/nonhydro-read/body-field-recovery/body-cached.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 18801,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 700,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 358,
        "paragraph_id": null,
        "text": "(2.2)"
      }
    ],
    "following_nonempty_paragraphs": [
      {
        "container_path": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/nonhydro-read/body-field-recovery/body-cached.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 18887,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 702,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 360,
        "paragraph_id": null,
        "text": "These solutions are similar to the dispersion relations present in lower order Boussinesq models (Dingemans, 1997)."
      },
      {
        "container_path": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/nonhydro-read/body-field-recovery/body-cached.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 18923,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 704,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 362,
        "paragraph_id": null,
        "text": "In Figure 4-9 these relations are compared to the expression from linear wave theory. For small values of kd the expression (2.1) - (2.3) approximate linear wave theory well. For kd<1 the relative error remains approximately below the 5%. However for kd>1  the error grows rapidly and the equations are no longer a good approximation to linear wave theory. For these shorter waves a higher resolution in the vertical is required."
      }
    ],
    "table_cell": null,
    "text_method": "Saved display-field substitution plus w:t; equation objects are not transcribed."
